{% comment %}
  Fonts — Cormorant Garamond for display, Lato for body, Material Symbols
  for icons. All three are self-hosted out of assets/ instead of fetched
  from fonts.googleapis.com.

  Two reasons. The Google stylesheets were render-blocking and lived on a
  second origin, so first paint waited on a DNS lookup, a TLS handshake and
  a stylesheet round trip before the browser had even asked for a font.
  And the icon font Google returns for that Material Symbols axis query is
  the entire 4,284-glyph variable family — 3.9 MB on every page, competing
  with the hero image for a phone's bandwidth. It was over half the weight
  of the site.

  The icon font here is that same font subset to the symbol names that
  appear anywhere in this theme, with GRAD and opsz pinned and wght cut to
  300–400 — the only two instances theme.css renders (.mi and .mi.mi-f):
  61 KB. Ligatures survive the subset, so the markup stays
  <span class="mi">shopping_bag</span> and no section had to change. Run
  scripts/build-icon-font.py after introducing an icon the theme has never
  used, or it paints as its own name in plain text.

  Cormorant Garamond ships from Google as one variable file per subset
  covering 300–700, so the four weights the theme asks for are a single
  download rather than four. Lato ships 100/300/400/700/900: no 500 and no
  600, which are the two weights the body copy leans on (49 and 93 rules).
  Those are left as authored — CSS font matching answers 500 with 400 and
  600 with 700, and measured on the served woff2 those land within 4% of
  the stems they replace. So only 400, 700 and italic 400 are fetched.

  The latin-ext faces are declared but only downloaded if a character in
  that range is actually rendered; the unicode-range values are Google's
  own, carried over verbatim. The three faces above the fold on every
  template — display, body, icons — are preloaded; the rest are left for
  the CSS to ask for. The password page draws no icons, so it renders
  this with preload_icons: false and skips that third preload.
{% endcomment %}
<link rel="preload" href="{{ 'cormorant-garamond-latin.woff2' | asset_url }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" href="{{ 'lato-400-latin.woff2' | asset_url }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
{%- unless preload_icons == false -%}
  <link rel="preload" href="{{ 'material-symbols-subset.woff2' | asset_url }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
{%- endunless -%}
